0.120 0.120 0.120 rg
/F1 10.50 Tf
1 0 0 1 74.00 393.50 Tm
(Nadia could have sold a dozen different things - she baked, she crafted, she was great with) Tj
/F1 10.50 Tf
1 0 0 1 74.00 378.00 Tm
(spreadsheets, and she spoke three languages. That was exactly her problem: she kept starting all) Tj
/F1 10.50 Tf
1 0 0 1 74.00 362.50 Tm
(four at once and finishing none. Overwhelmed, she almost gave up. Her mentor gave her a single) Tj
/F1 10.50 Tf
1 0 0 1 74.00 347.00 Tm
(instruction: "Pick ONE. Give it ninety days. Then judge." She chose her celebration cakes - the) Tj
/F1 10.50 Tf
1 0 0 1 74.00 331.50 Tm
(thing neighbors already begged her for. With all her energy in one place, she booked her first paid) Tj
/F1 10.50 Tf
1 0 0 1 74.00 316.00 Tm
(order in a week and had a small waitlist by month three. The other ideas didn't die; they just) Tj
/F1 10.50 Tf
1 0 0 1 74.00 300.50 Tm
(waited their turn. Focus, not talent, was the unlock.) Tj
0.000 0.000 0.000 rg
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 270.00 Tm
(Once your brain dump is full of possibilities, the beginner's trap is trying to do all of them. Spreading) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 253.50 Tm
(yourself thin is the fastest route to finishing nothing. Your job now is to pick one first offer and commit) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 237.00 Tm
(to it.) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 214.50 Tm
(Score each idea against four simple questions:) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 192.00 Tm
