(The $5 Mistake) Tj
0.120 0.120 0.120 rg
/F1 10.50 Tf
1 0 0 1 74.00 683.00 Tm
(When Sam started editing videos from home, terror made him cheap - he charged $5 an edit, sure) Tj
/F1 10.50 Tf
1 0 0 1 74.00 667.50 Tm
(no one would pay more. Clients flooded in, and he nearly collapsed: after hours of work and the) Tj
/F1 10.50 Tf
1 0 0 1 74.00 652.00 Tm
(cost of his software, he was earning less than minimum wage and too swamped to find better) Tj
/F1 10.50 Tf
1 0 0 1 74.00 636.50 Tm
(clients. A blunt customer finally told him, "Your work is worth ten times this." Shaking, he raised) Tj
/F1 10.50 Tf
1 0 0 1 74.00 621.00 Tm
(his price to $50. He lost the bargain-hunters - and kept the serious clients who valued quality. He) Tj
/F1 10.50 Tf
1 0 0 1 74.00 605.50 Tm
(worked fewer hours for more money, and finally had time to grow. Underpricing hadn't protected) Tj
/F1 10.50 Tf
1 0 0 1 74.00 590.00 Tm
(him; it had nearly buried him.) Tj
0.000 0.000 0.000 rg
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 559.50 Tm
(Nothing scares beginners like pricing - so they guess, usually too low. Let's replace fear with a) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 543.00 Tm
(simple truth: if you don't know your profit margin, you don't have a business - you have an expensive) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 526.50 Tm
(hobby.) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 504.00 Tm
(Profit margin is just what's left after costs. For each unit of what you sell:) Tj
0.720 0.470 0.100 rg
/F2 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 74.00 467.50 Tm
(Price ? Costs = Profit. Costs include materials, software/tools, fees, and - crucially -) Tj
/F2 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 74.00 452.00 Tm
(your time.) Tj
0.000 0.000 0.000 rg
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 421.50 Tm
(Two beginner traps to avoid:) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 399.00 Tm
(1. Forgetting to pay yourself. If a job takes you five hours, your price must cover five hours of your) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 382.50 Tm
(time plus costs, or you're paying to work. Know how long one unit takes.) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 360.00 Tm
(2. Pricing from fear. Charging rock-bottom rates attracts the most demanding, least loyal customers) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 343.50 Tm
(and leaves no room to breathe. A fair, confident price attracts clients who value quality - and lets) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 327.00 Tm
(your business survive.) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 60.00 304.50 Tm
(How to set a starting price:) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 76.00 283.00 Tm
(- Research the going rate. What do others charge for similar work? Land in a sensible range, not) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 76.00 267.50 Tm
(    the bargain basement.) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 76.00 252.00 Tm
(- Add up your true costs per unit \(including your hourly time\).) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 76.00 236.50 Tm
(- Make sure price comfortably beats cost - that gap is your profit and your future.) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
1 0 0 1 76.00 221.00 Tm
(- Start a bit higher than feels comfortable. It's far easier to offer a discount than to raise a price you) Tj
/F1 11.00 Tf
